 34P  c  Compiled (unevaluated) data set from 2012Be11:                         
 34P 2c  Phys Rev C 85, 044305 (2102); and 2011BeZZ:                            
 34P 3c  Priv. comm. received May 17, 2011                                      
 34P  c  Compiled from 2011BeZZ by M. Birch and B. Singh (McMaster);            
 34P 2c  May 30, 2011.                                                          
 34P  c  Edited by B. Singh. June 9, 2011, to document half-life                
 34P  c  Updated by N. Nica (Texas A&M) and B. Singh (McMaster) to include      
 34P 2c  data from 2012Be11; Apr 5, 2012.                                       
 34P  c  See also 2009Be26: Phys Rev C 80, 014302 from the same group           
 34P  c  All data given here are from 2012Be11                                  
 34P  c  24 MeV {+18}O beam produced using the Argonne Tandem-Linac             
 34P 2c  Accelerator System(ATLAS) impinged on a 260 |mg/cm{+2} thick {+18}O    
 34P 3c  target enriched to 97% with Ta backing surrounded by a nearly 4|p      
 34P 4c  array of 95 CsI(Tl) scintillators to detect charged particles.         
 34P 5c  The |g-rays detected by Gammasphere array consisting of about 101      
 34P 6c  Compton suppressed HPGe detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g,            
 34P 7c  (particle)|g coin, |g(|q), lifetimes with DSAM and lineshapes.         
 34P 8c  Comparisons with shell-model calculations.                             
 34P  cG MR$ Sign convention is that of Rose and Brink in 2012Be11. The         
 34P 2cG compilers have used Krane-Steffen convention, thus each sign in        
 34P 3cG 2012Be11 is reversed here                                              
